      * T0EDS - harness probe: E-spec compile-time array + DS subfields.
      * Confirms tools/gen/rpg3.mjs eSpec/compileTimeArrayData/iSpecDS/
      * iSpecSubfield column positions against a real CRTRPGPGM compile.
      * 2026-09-26, real-hardware fix: the ** + data lines must be the
      * LAST thing in the source, after the O-specs (rpg400ref.txt
      * "Loading a Compile-Time Array": "enter array input data into
      * records ... following the source records for this program").
      * An earlier version had them between the C-specs and O-specs;
      * PUB400 then read the array data records as still more O-spec
      * text (QRG8041 "too many entries"), and the real O-specs after
      * that point were never recognized at all (QRG7064 "file not
      * referenced", QRG7026 "no unnamed EXCPT output"). The O-spec
      * column layout itself (E at col15) was never the problem - it
      * matches every already-verified Part 4 source (R0401A etc.).
